  "description": "Braid-word basis Gram-matrix probe at H_3(q_0). Computes G_wv = tr_M(σ_w · σ_v) for the 6-element reduced-word basis {e, σ_0, σ_1, σ_0σ_1, σ_1σ_0, σ_0σ_1σ_0} via the Wenzl bridge Σ_λ y_λ · tr_{V_λ}(ρ_λ(...)) and Hoefsmit seminormal matrices. Demonstrates that the paper-canonical σ_w basis (CLAUDE.md §7a) has GENUINE off-diagonal Gram entries — the structural property the per-partition basis lacks by Wedderburn orthogonality. The SDP shadow-price hypothesis is testable non-degenerately in this basis. Class C (diagnostic / structural). Substrate-only (CAL-2 q_0); no CAL-3 input.",
